  "limits": [
    "Damage/health packet retention is limited to public fields recorded by the driver; absence is not absence of server damage. Pending attack windows may overlap; receipt dedup uses traceActor, receiver, sequence and packet.",
    "Final HP/MP cannot be invented from ObjectHealth percentage or absent HealthChanged records. Owner snapshots are action-start observations, not continuous health telemetry.",
    "UserLocation target is recipient global ID. Local1000 is never a global mapping or an automatic cross-client actor match.",
    "Gateway trace IDs group server stages only. No client trace ID exists; latency is producer-to-send/flush, not client receive.",
    "read_gate and completion_to_pop recordedUnixMs may be delayed emission: do not subtract duration to establish exact intervals. health stages overlap and must not be added.",
    "normalDepth/ownerDepth are dequeue snapshots. completion_to_pop includes idle receive waits; a long duration does not alone prove backlog.",
    "A stale or delayed presentation diagnosis requires packet/health evidence, not merely coincidence with a slow span.",
    "Strict allowlists discard text, account/auth/password fields and runtime JSON. Unknown schema types are marked other; raw originals are not re-read."
  ]
}
